help-files-format = Ugurugu 3 saves projects as .ugurugu files.
help-files-tabs = Each project opens in a tab above the canvas, and a project opened from File Explorer opens as a tab of the window already open. Ctrl+Tab moves to the next tab and Ctrl+W closes one.
help-files-import = Projects saved as .ugu by Ugurugu 2.1.0 or later open as new projects and are saved as .ugurugu. The .ugu file is not changed.
help-files-older = Older .ugu files and .wagle, .wobble and .wawa files open in Ugurugu 2.2.13. Save older .ugu files there again to open them here.
help-install = Installing and updates
help-install-beside = Ugurugu 3 installs as its own app beside Ugurugu 2, with its own settings and recovery files. Both can stay installed.
help-install-smartscreen = The installer is not code-signed, so Windows may say it does not recognize it. Choose More info and then Run anyway, and download the installer only from the project's GitHub Releases page.
help-install-updates = Ugurugu checks for updates when it starts, at most every six hours; turn this off in Settings > General. Help > Check for Updates… checks now. An update installs once the window closes, after asking to save your changes.
help-problems = Reporting a problem
help-problems-logs = Ugurugu keeps log files of its recent runs and tells you on the next start if it closed unexpectedly. Settings > About opens the log folder and copies diagnostic info to attach to a GitHub issue. Nothing is sent automatically.
